WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.360
SPEAKER 1: I've worked at
Hillsdale College for a little

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.250
over 20 years now, which
is hard to believe.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.390
But it's been a lot of fun
to watch the college grow

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.340
and extend its reach
nationwide, guided all the while

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:20.400
by the college's original
1844 founding mission.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.530
As our trustee Chris
Bachelder mentioned,

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.980
on campus, the quality of
the faculty and the students

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.230
is better than ever.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.009
And off campus, more Americans
learn from Hillsdale College

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:36.990
than ever before, just
think of the more than 5.6

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:41.160
million readers of Imprimis
or the more than 2.5

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.000
million Americans who have
signed up and taken one or more

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.460
of our online courses.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.960
While we go about
our work every day

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.918
at Hillsdale under the
direction and leadership

00:00:50.918 --> 00:00:53.760
of our next speaker,
he's been the pilot

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:00.210
of the Hillsdale College ship
for almost 21 years this year.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.670
He's a scholar of
Winston Churchill.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.480
He's a prolific and
best-selling author.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.950
He's a professor of
history and politics,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.420
including a recent course
on totalitarian novels.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.600
You may not know that he's
also a big fan of baseball

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.370
and tennis.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.310
And he's an avid motorcyclist.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.970
In recent years, he's
led a two-wheeled gang

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.490
on a big summer road trip.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.680
I don't know where
they're going this year.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.570
But he may tell us.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.280
Would you please
welcome to the podium,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.238
the 12th president of Hillsdale
College, Larry P. Arnn.

00:01:36.238 --> 00:01:39.232
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.990
LARRY ARNN: Thank you, Tim.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.790
This year we're
going to the Ozarks.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.325
Because I'm from Arkansas, and
I want to see all my cousins.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.850
If you think 2020
was bad, wait till it

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.395
turns 21 and starts drinking.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.410
Kathy Kramer, where's Kathy?

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.660
Hold up your hand Kathy.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:25.630
Yeah, she's ordered me to
give you reason for optimism.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.580
So I'm going to say
a bunch of bad stuff.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.740
There are things to worry about.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.700
We're suffering from
a mental pandemic.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.740
And that has caused
them to interfere

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:47.090
with the rights of
millions of Americans,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.590
destroyed their businesses.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.480
Our governor in Michigan, a
brilliant stateswoman she is,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:56.980
too.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.990
She spends her days,
you know, she's

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.740
got more than 1,000
pages of rules.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.100
And they're
contradictory and stupid.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.310
And the first thing is, if
you know how to run anything,

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.478
you know rules are
always a bad idea.

00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:20.270
You know, when I came
to Hillsdale College,

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.780
we had 134 pages
of student rules.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.820
Now we have 17 rules, not
pages of rules, rules, right.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.560
And that means we
can kind of know

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.780
what they are, although 17 is
too many to carry in your mind.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:39.620
The one great rule
is behave yourself.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.240
Be good.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.150
They swear an oath and an
honor code to do that, right.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.700
And that's really the
only rule you need.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.290
But she's like that, right.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:54.660
And she has messed
with our college.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.800
Right now, the score is
Hillsdale, 3, governor, 0.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.638
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.550
But it's irksome.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.060
Because, you know, somebody--

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.550
some supposed right-wingers
that disappeared

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.660
when they found out
they were Antifa people

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.500
had a plot to kidnap her.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.740
And so I was asked
by a journalist,

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.730
would you know anybody
who'd want to do that?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.496
And I said, I don't know anybody
who'd even like to meet her.

00:04:27.496 --> 00:04:29.976
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.660
See, that's optimism, Kathy.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:43.320
That's a tragic thing I'm
describing, but it's funny,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.976
you know.

00:04:44.976 --> 00:04:49.318
The election was a mass of
corruption and disorder.

00:04:49.318 --> 00:04:53.500
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.360
Tomorrow, I'm going to tell you
about some state legislators

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.810
in an unnamed state that might
be one that I would know a lot

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.410
about, whatever state that was.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.880
And it will make you sad.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.690
Also, it will show
us what to do.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.520
And now, the government
is in the hands

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.400
of radical liberalism.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.140
Oh, I got to have my prop.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:23.230
Grace, bring me that
book over there.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.296
This is the great Grace Balkan.

00:05:26.296 --> 00:05:30.080
[APPLAUSE]

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.100
Oh yeah, also that--

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:38.300
the prayer girl, Taryn Murphy,
outstanding senior woman,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.730
and she is dating
the useless Grant

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:45.830
Wood who's about to go
into the Marine Corps.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.680
And I think now that
she's reached her glory,

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.441
she'll see better than that.

00:05:50.441 --> 00:05:53.267
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.920
Actually, Grant is a very
fine young man just unworthy

00:05:58.920 --> 00:05:59.430
of Taryn.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.140
So on the first day of
the Biden administration,

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.240
we were up first.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:16.130
He canceled the 1776 Commission
and erased the report

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:18.140
from the White House.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:22.310
They were mad at it
because we had five weeks

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.540
to form a commission, have
meetings, write a report,

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:31.490
agree to it unanimously,
and then design, publish it,

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.140
and get it out.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.630
And we were destroyed because
the government doesn't

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.460
like things to move like that.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.907
But now it's been completely
obliterated, except wait--

00:06:43.907 --> 00:06:46.402
[APPLAUSE]

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.730
It's just been published
by Encounter Books.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.250
And we've added footnotes.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.920
And the footnotes
are to two things.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.730
They're to original
source documents,

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.580
and they are to leading
historians, some of whom

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.060
have attacked us, who say
exactly the same thing

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.790
in their own books.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.700
So that'll be fun.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:13.492
It's a little book.

00:07:13.492 --> 00:07:15.330
You should get it.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.950
Write me, and I'll
send it to you.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.200
Also Joe Biden is
the honorary chair

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.520
of our marketing campaign.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:23.922
[LAUGHTER]

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.974
At last, somewhere
where he's effective.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:40.720
The worst thing of
all is they're messing

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.500
with the electoral system.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.350
And I'll talk about
that some tomorrow.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.360
But the truth is, in
a representative form

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:52.370
of government, the linchpin
of it, the crucial point,

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.920
is the voting system.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:58.180
And so I believe that
in the Obama years

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:03.850
they figured out
that, unexpectedly,

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:07.670
people don't actually
like what they do.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.223
And so they might have reformed
and moderated themselves.

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:12.640
But instead what
they did was they

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.970
decided we're
going to make them.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.790
And I think we're living
under that effort right now.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.200
So that's the bad stuff.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.220
How am I doing, Kathy?

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:31.090
But I know three pieces of
delightful news, powerful news.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.870
Two, I'm going to tell you right
now and the other one tomorrow.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:41.190
The first one is Hillsdale
College is just thriving.

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.860
It's just marvelous to us.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:49.200
[APPLAUSE]

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.730
And we're stubborn cusses.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.160
And we're not given to
counting our successes.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.770
Because when we're
dead, we can do that.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:09:00.210
But, you know, it's been
successful for a long time.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:01.470
Now it's more.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.940
It's just amazing.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.380
Like our entering
class next year

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.520
is going to have an entering
standardized test score

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:15.970
one point below the Ivy League.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.780
So it's about 25th
in the country.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:20.685
And--

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:22.960
[APPLAUSE]

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.530
And we could fill up another
college at those standards now.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:30.170
And everything is like that.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.710
You've been very
generous with us.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.710
Thank you very much.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.930
Our students are
now paying about 7%

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.060
of the budget of
Hillsdale College.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:41.525
And that means we don't need
them, and we can tell them so.

00:09:41.525 --> 00:09:46.430
[LAUGHTER] And that's
really good for them.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.678
Because, you know,
they'll be spoiled babies

00:09:48.678 --> 00:09:49.720
if we don't torture them.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.050
Do you know how many
people get Imprimis?

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:03.920
Almost six million,
isn't that crazy?

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:09.890
And do you know many people have
registered for online courses

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:14.180
at Hillsdale College in the
last, what is it, 8 or 9 years?

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:24.130
Almost three million, growing
faster now than previously.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.450
And what are those
courses, right?

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.710
The latest one is Euclid.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.010
It's already got 10,000
people taking it.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:36.530
Aristotle, Dante is
coming soon, right.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.060
What-- isn't that an
amazing phenomenon?

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:43.030
I get recognized
in airports now.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.690
And-- and people walk up
to me, and they talk to me

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:50.650
like they're students,
just like on the campus.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:51.550
Oh, you're Dr. Arnn.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.508
And I say, yes, indeed.

00:10:52.508 --> 00:10:55.840
And he says, well, we
just love your course.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:01.240
And I say, are you
taking the exams?

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.730
And they do exactly
what students do.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:06.856
They look at their feet
and kind of shuffle around.

00:11:06.856 --> 00:11:10.395
[LAUGHING] They're afraid I'm
going to look up their score.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.810
That's all good news.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:22.470
And I submit to you, Kathy
Kramer, world-changing news.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.860
Just remember, all the best
things, every great thing

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.460
ever done in human
history is done

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:34.496
by a volunteer and somebody
who does it for love.

00:11:34.496 --> 00:11:37.370
[APPLAUSE]

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:47.380
Second great news tonight
is our speaker tonight.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:50.262
Somewhere near the
center of our problems,

00:11:50.262 --> 00:11:51.970
I'll talking about
this a little tomorrow

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:55.050
because I learned it
from Winston Churchill,

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:59.520
is the corruption of the ancient
and natural way of knowing

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.530
called natural science.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.980
It's a beautiful thing.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:07.150
We know more about the
material and the natural world

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:09.490
than we ever have.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.500
But the weight of
those disciplines

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.430
has turned not from science--

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:17.930
from science, it just means
knowing in Latin to technology,

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:20.460
which means making.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.670
And making is not the
same thing as knowing.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:27.800
Making is an exercise in power.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:32.310
So it's no accident
that we are governed

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:36.760
by supposedly scientists.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:42.200
I mean, I can talk all day
about the governor of Michigan.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.320
I've still managed-- if she
was beating me, I would--

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.950
it'd be heart rending to me.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:51.780
But so far, we're doing pretty
good, so I can talk about her.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:57.860
She was asked, there are, what,
40,000 or 50,000, Scott Atlas

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:01.160
will know, medical
researchers and some

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:04.580
of the many of the leading
epidemiologists in the world

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:06.920
who've signed the Great
Barrington Declaration, which

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:10.310
says, this is all crazy.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:14.050
You know, Facebook took
it down the other day.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.890
I had an argument with a medical
doctor, a friend, a good guy,

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.330
at the Mayo Clinic.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.630
And he said, well, you're
using the epidemiologists that

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:24.650
are for opening up.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.720
And I said, correct.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.410
And he said, you
knew that already.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.410
And I said, yeah, what
do you think I'm running,

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.960
a scientific experiment here?

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.510
I'm running a college.

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.700
It's my duty to have college.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:40.220
It's my duty to find
a way that's safe.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:42.680
Because, as I tell the
students all the time,

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.120
if you get sick
and die from this,

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.383
it's going to be very
inconvenient to me.

00:13:46.383 --> 00:13:49.655
[LAUGHTER]

00:13:49.655 --> 00:13:50.780
Which, you know, it's true.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:53.300
And I have a stake in
protecting them, right.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:56.510
But on the other hand, my
job is to have college.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:14:00.120
So this doctor, who's got
kids at Hillsdale College

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.090
and came to our commencement.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.310
I said, you've just
proved my point.

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.060
And he said, how?

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:08.120
And I said, you guys are the
best in the world at Mayo

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.635
Clinic, aren't you?

00:14:09.635 --> 00:14:10.760
He said, we're pretty good.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.490
And I said, how about
these guys at Stanford?

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.780
Are they pretty good?

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.340
And he says, yeah.

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:21.110
And I said, see,
you don't agree.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:24.510
Experts never do about
a practical judgment.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:28.110
They will, by the way,
eventually reach an agreement

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.940
about the facts
that can be measured

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:32.440
if they're any use at all.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.250
But this thing about what
to do about this pandemic

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.250
when you have the
power to shut down

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:42.600
the largest economy in
the history of the world.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.030
That's a thing of massive and
incalculable consequences.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.993
And nobody can be
an expert in that.

00:14:49.993 --> 00:14:51.660
And he said, well,
you got a good point.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.350
And I said, thank you very much.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:59.120
And on the other
hand, I did need

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:02.300
to know if I was going
to kill these kids.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:06.960
Because I say, it'd just cause
me a world of trouble if I did.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:10.340
Where'd I learn that?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.750
Three people, one of
them our speaker tonight.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:20.180
Three top people, and three
people, who it turns out,

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:22.240
are brave.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.600
Because they stood
up against this.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.370
Their names, or the
ones who helped us,

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:32.430
are Jay Bhattacharya
from Stanford

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:37.320
and Daniel Halperin from
North Carolina and then,

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:41.406
the toughest of them all, Scott
Atlas, our speaker tonight.

00:15:41.406 --> 00:15:46.270
[CHEERING]

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:50.440
And, you know, a great,
intellectual argument

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:55.500
is always some wisdom of
intellectual and moral power.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:58.230
Because you have to be
brave to speak the truth

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.780
in the face of consequences.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.360
Scott Atlas is one of
the leading physicians

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.100
in the world.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:10.290
He wrote the book on
magnetic resonance imaging

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:12.690
of the brain and the spine.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:15.510
And somehow, in the
course of writing on that,

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:21.960
he delivered-- he developed
both and he's just strong.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:25.200
He did work for the
president, for President Trump

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:26.580
for a while.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:32.980
And the point is, it's
such a violent culture

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.920
today that for a
leading scientist

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:40.840
to offer his counsel to the
President of the United States,

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:44.140
when there are people
dying as there are,

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:47.850
and that is a disgrace.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:52.420
That tells you where
the country is.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:17:00.290
I say, he's a
cause for optimism.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:04.710
Because I didn't know him
before any of this came up.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.760
And so that means that I, and
all of us, every one of us,

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:12.290
has discovered a brave
and brilliant man.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:15.500
And the only correct
conclusion to draw from that

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:18.650
is there must be more.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:21.829
And we are stronger
by knowing him.

00:17:21.829 --> 00:17:23.338
Please come up here Scott.

00:17:23.338 --> 00:17:26.272
[APPLAUSE]

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.120
As you know, Hillsdale
College is very old, not long

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.420
in the tooth.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.690
And there's an award
that I'm about to give

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:49.850
Scott we've been giving
here for more than 40 years.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.490
And we've given it
to Ronald Reagan.

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.157
And we've given it
to Margaret Thatcher.

00:17:53.157 --> 00:17:55.450
And we've given it
to Clarence Thomas

00:17:55.450 --> 00:18:00.470
and some other small names.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:04.040
And it's called the
Freedom Leadership Award.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:08.060
And that means leadership
which takes courage

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.430
toward freedom, which
has a generosity

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.520
to everyone it touches.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.956
I'm proud to present this
award to Scott Atlas.

00:18:16.956 --> 00:18:19.932
[APPLAUSE]

00:18:45.332 --> 00:18:46.290
SCOTT ATLAS: Thank you.

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.450
Thank you so much.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:51.180
Thank you President Arnn,
supporters of Hillsdale,

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:54.480
and Hillsdale National
Leadership Seminar Program,

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.140
and members of this
distinguished audience.

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.910
It's a great honor to be here.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.380
It's my first
exposure to Hillsdale.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.610
And it's awesome.

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:08.069
I am really thrilled to be here.

00:19:08.069 --> 00:19:12.860
[APPLAUSE]

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.730
I'm very, very grateful
to receive the award.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:20.380
I'm, of course, highly honored
to be on the list of winners.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.690
And I sincerely
thank everyone who

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:25.550
had anything to do with this.

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:29.410
It's also great to be in a crowd
that is friendly for a change.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:35.040
[LAUGHTER]

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.770
Hillsdale's National
Leadership Seminar Program,

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:39.900
as everyone here
knows, was founded

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.420
with a specific mission,
quote, to foster

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:45.630
enlightened leadership and
informed decision-making

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:48.840
for America's third
century, by communicating

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.830
the fundamental principles
of freedom and order

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:57.450
on which Western civilization
is based, unquote.

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.790
The pandemic has been
a tragedy, no doubt.

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:04.470
But it has exposed
profound issues in America

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:08.700
that now threaten those very
principles of freedom and order

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.800
that we Americans too
often take for granted.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:19.720
First, I must say I was
shocked at the enormous power

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:22.810
of the government to
unilaterally decree

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:25.930
to simply close
businesses and schools,

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:29.710
restrict personal movement,
mandate behavior, eliminate

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:34.510
our most basic freedoms
without any end.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:38.950
And second, I was,
and I remain, stunned

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:43.120
and a little bit frightened
at the acquiescence

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:47.050
of the American people to these
destructive, arbitrary, and

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:51.124
wholly unscientific rules,
restrictions, and mandates.

00:20:51.124 --> 00:20:53.494
[APPLAUSE]

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:01.630
This crisis also exposed
what we have all known

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.730
existed, but we tolerated.

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:06.460
Although I think Hillsdale
didn't tolerate it

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.890
as much as everyone else.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:13.000
But the rest of the
country tolerated for years

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.360
the bias of the media, the
suppression of academic freedom

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:20.150
on campuses, the lack of
neutrality in big tech,

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:23.050
and now, more
obviously than ever,

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:26.320
the politicization of science.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:29.710
Ultimately, the freedom to
seek and state the truth

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:32.110
is at risk here in
the United States.

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:40.480
First, we all acknowledge
the consequences of the SARS2

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.830
coronavirus pandemic and its
management have been enormous.

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:47.170
Over 500,000
American deaths have

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:48.710
been attributed to the virus.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:51.340
More will certainly follow.

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:55.550
Even after a year, the pandemic
still paralyzes our country.

00:21:55.550 --> 00:22:00.040
And despite all efforts, there
has been an undeniable failure

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:03.400
to stop the cases from rapidly
escalating and preventing

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:05.470
hospitalizations and death.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.750
But here's the
unacknowledged reality.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:10.810
Almost every state
and major city

00:22:10.810 --> 00:22:14.230
has implemented severe
restrictions for many months,

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:17.650
including closures of businesses
and in-person schools,

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:21.550
mobility restrictions, curfews,
quarantines, limits on groups

00:22:21.550 --> 00:22:25.060
and families, and mask
mandates dating back to

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:26.980
at least the summer.

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.530
And let's clear up the
myths about the behavior

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:30.700
of Americans.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:34.450
Social mobility tracking and
data from Gallup, YouGov,

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:37.240
the COVID-19
Consortium, and the CDC

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:40.330
have shown significant
reductions of movement,

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:42.760
as well as consistently
high percentage

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:45.670
of mask wearing since
late last summer,

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:49.330
similar to Western Europe
and approaching that in Asia.

00:22:49.330 --> 00:22:52.750
There is no truth to the fact
that these mandates were not

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.460
obeyed.

00:22:54.460 --> 00:22:58.570
All legitimate
policy scholars today

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:01.120
should be re-examining
policies that severely

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:04.390
harmed Americans
families and children

00:23:04.390 --> 00:23:07.150
and failed to save the elderly.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.720
Numerous studies, including
one from my current institution

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:14.020
Stanford University's
infectious disease scientists

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:18.550
and epidemiologists Bendavid,
Oh, Bhattacharya, and Ioannidis

00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:21.730
have shown the mitigating impact
of these extraordinary measures

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:25.840
used in almost every
state was small at best.

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.780
President Biden openly
admitted this lack of efficacy

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:32.080
in his speech on January
22 when he said, quote,

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:34.000
there is nothing
we can do to change

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:36.970
the trajectory of the pandemic
in the next several months,

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:38.470
unquote.

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:41.470
Bizarrely though,
many want to blame

00:23:41.470 --> 00:23:45.730
those who oppose the lockdowns
an the mandates for the failure

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:47.800
of the lockdowns and
the mandates that

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:49.330
were widely implemented.

00:23:53.690 --> 00:23:56.570
Separate from their
limited value efficacy that

00:23:56.570 --> 00:24:01.580
has been grossly exaggerated
in scientific journals,

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:05.570
lockdown policies have been
extraordinarily harmful.

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:08.570
The harms to children of
closing in-person schools

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:11.120
are dramatic, poor
learning, school dropouts,

00:24:11.120 --> 00:24:15.410
social isolation, suicidal
ideation, most of which

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:19.370
are far worse for
lower income families.

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:22.880
A recent study confirms
up to 78% of cancers

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:26.070
were never detected due to
missed screen over three

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:26.570
months.

00:24:26.570 --> 00:24:29.150
And extrapolating to
the entire country,

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:32.780
over a million new cases
over 9 months of cancer

00:24:32.780 --> 00:24:35.000
will have gone undetected.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:37.580
That disaster adds
to missed surgeries,

00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:40.670
delayed presentations of
pediatric illnesses, heart

00:24:40.670 --> 00:24:43.640
attack, and stroke patients
too afraid to call emergency

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:48.260
services, and others,
all well documented.

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:52.370
Beyond hospital care, the CDC
reported fourfold increases

00:24:52.370 --> 00:24:55.940
in depression, tripling of
anxiety symptoms, doubling

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:57.980
of suicidal ideation,
particularly

00:24:57.980 --> 00:25:00.620
among young adults.

00:25:00.620 --> 00:25:03.590
After the first few
months of lockdowns,

00:25:03.590 --> 00:25:06.200
domestic abuse, child
abuse skyrocketing

00:25:06.200 --> 00:25:08.030
due to the isolation
and, specifically,

00:25:08.030 --> 00:25:12.290
to the loss of jobs,
particularly in strict lockdown

00:25:12.290 --> 00:25:14.100
states.

00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:16.250
Given that many in-person
schools have closed,

00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:19.820
hundreds of thousands of child
abuse cases are not reported.

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:24.680
Because schools are where child
abuse is most frequently noted.

00:25:24.680 --> 00:25:27.350
Finally, the unemployment
shock from the lockdowns,

00:25:27.350 --> 00:25:30.440
according to a
recent NBER study,

00:25:30.440 --> 00:25:36.080
will generate almost 890,000
additional US deaths,

00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:38.870
mainly in minority
and poor families,

00:25:38.870 --> 00:25:40.280
over the next 15 years.

00:25:40.280 --> 00:25:44.070
That's the lockdown alone.

00:25:44.070 --> 00:25:46.790
We know we have not seen the
full extent of the damage.

00:25:46.790 --> 00:25:48.720
Because it will
last for decades.

00:25:48.720 --> 00:25:51.440
Perhaps that is why
lockdowns were never

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:54.950
recommended in previous
pandemic analysis,

00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:59.270
even for infections with
far higher death rates.

00:25:59.270 --> 00:26:01.160
To determine the
best path forward,

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:04.040
shouldn't policymakers
now objectively

00:26:04.040 --> 00:26:08.360
consider both the virus harms
and the totality of impact

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:11.210
of the policies to date?

00:26:11.210 --> 00:26:15.620
That's the importance of health
policy experts, my field.

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:18.440
We have a broader
scope of expertise

00:26:18.440 --> 00:26:22.070
than that of epidemiologists
and basic scientists,

00:26:22.070 --> 00:26:26.000
who you see on TV every day.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.460
And that necessarily
means admitting

00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:31.550
that social lockdowns and
significant restrictions

00:26:31.550 --> 00:26:34.970
on individuals are
deadly, extraordinarily

00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:37.760
harmful, especially
on the working class

00:26:37.760 --> 00:26:40.160
minorities and the poor.

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:41.870
Optimistically, we
should be seeing

00:26:41.870 --> 00:26:43.670
the light at the end
of the long tunnel

00:26:43.670 --> 00:26:46.170
now with the vaccine rollout.

00:26:46.170 --> 00:26:49.070
On the other hand,
using logic that

00:26:49.070 --> 00:26:52.610
would put Alice in Wonderland's
Mat Hatter to shame,

00:26:52.610 --> 00:26:56.000
the new vaccines were first
more frequently administered

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:58.940
to healthier, younger
people, instead of those

00:26:58.940 --> 00:27:01.820
at risk to die in most states.

00:27:01.820 --> 00:27:05.690
And now we hear children must be
vaccinated before schools open

00:27:05.690 --> 00:27:08.720
when they have extremely
low risk from this infection

00:27:08.720 --> 00:27:11.690
and are proven to not
be significant spreaders

00:27:11.690 --> 00:27:13.490
to adults.

00:27:13.490 --> 00:27:16.520
Or the Kafkaesque
nonsense that teachers

00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:20.240
must be vaccinated before
they teach in person, when

00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:22.820
schools are one of the
lowest risk environments.

00:27:22.820 --> 00:27:26.810
And the vast majority of
teachers are not high risk.

00:27:26.810 --> 00:27:31.760
Even worse, we hear the same
old so-called experts on TV

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:34.820
now warning that social
distancing, masks,

00:27:34.820 --> 00:27:36.500
and other restrictions
will still

00:27:36.500 --> 00:27:40.130
be necessary after vaccines.

00:27:40.130 --> 00:27:43.850
There is no intention
of those in power

00:27:43.850 --> 00:27:48.080
to allow Americans to live
normally, to live freely again,

00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:50.776
and don't ever think otherwise.

00:27:50.776 --> 00:27:53.734
[APPLAUSE]

00:27:58.180 --> 00:28:03.050
Just as in Galileo's time, the
real problem is what he called,

00:28:03.050 --> 00:28:07.120
quote, vested academic
interests, unquote.

00:28:07.120 --> 00:28:11.620
Many universities, which
should be America's centers

00:28:11.620 --> 00:28:15.550
for critical thinking, have
overtly intimidated views

00:28:15.550 --> 00:28:19.810
contrary to their own,
undoubtedly, undeniably out

00:28:19.810 --> 00:28:23.350
of political reasons, leaving
many afraid to speak up.

00:28:23.350 --> 00:28:27.190
I know, I get their emails for
months, people encouraging me

00:28:27.190 --> 00:28:28.645
but are afraid to step forward.

00:28:31.430 --> 00:28:34.070
But it is not only the
matter of academic freedom

00:28:34.070 --> 00:28:35.660
that needs comment.

00:28:35.660 --> 00:28:38.720
Instead of rethinking
the failed policies,

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:41.540
some Stanford
professors have chosen

00:28:41.540 --> 00:28:45.140
to employ toxic smears
and opinion pieces

00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:47.840
and organized rebukes
against those of us

00:28:47.840 --> 00:28:51.920
who disagreed with what was
implemented but worse who dared

00:28:51.920 --> 00:28:55.160
to help the country under
a president they despised,

00:28:55.160 --> 00:28:59.060
apparently the
ultimate transgression.

00:28:59.060 --> 00:29:02.180
Defamatory attacks
with malicious intent

00:29:02.180 --> 00:29:06.020
based on straw man arguments
and out of context distortions

00:29:06.020 --> 00:29:09.170
are not acceptable
in civilized society,

00:29:09.170 --> 00:29:11.420
let alone in our universities.

00:29:11.420 --> 00:29:14.070
In their attempt to
intimidate and discredit me

00:29:14.070 --> 00:29:17.210
using falsifications
and misrepresentations,

00:29:17.210 --> 00:29:21.560
a group of untruthful professors
violated, with impunity,

00:29:21.560 --> 00:29:25.370
Stanford's code of conduct,
damaged the Stanford name,

00:29:25.370 --> 00:29:29.030
and, most importantly, abused
the trust parents in society

00:29:29.030 --> 00:29:32.090
place in them to influence
America's children,

00:29:32.090 --> 00:29:34.730
our next generation of leaders.

00:29:34.730 --> 00:29:37.020
This is unacceptable.

00:29:37.020 --> 00:29:39.770
It is understandable that most
Stanford professors are not

00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:42.770
experts in my field,
health policy,

00:29:42.770 --> 00:29:46.940
and even that most are ignorant
of the data about the pandemic.

00:29:46.940 --> 00:29:48.800
But it is not
acceptable to claim

00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:51.350
I made recommendations that
were, quote, falsehoods

00:29:51.350 --> 00:29:53.600
and misrepresentations
of science.

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:55.480
That is a lie.

00:29:55.480 --> 00:29:58.940
And no matter how often a lie
is repeated and regardless

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:01.700
of how often those lies
are echoed in the media,

00:30:01.700 --> 00:30:04.700
lies do not transform
into truths.

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:08.030
We all must pray to God
that the phrase attributed

00:30:08.030 --> 00:30:11.480
to Nazi propagandist
Joseph Goebbels, quote,

00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:14.210
a lie told once remains
a lie, but a lie

00:30:14.210 --> 00:30:19.460
told 1,000 times becomes
the truth, unquote, never

00:30:19.460 --> 00:30:22.220
becomes true in these
United States of America.

00:30:22.220 --> 00:30:25.148
[APPLAUSE]

00:30:30.030 --> 00:30:33.300
All policy considerations I
recommended to the president

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:35.850
were designed to reduce
both the spread of the virus

00:30:35.850 --> 00:30:38.610
to the most vulnerable
and the harms to those

00:30:38.610 --> 00:30:41.340
impacted by the
policies the most,

00:30:41.340 --> 00:30:44.100
the poor and working
class of America.

00:30:44.100 --> 00:30:47.550
I was one of the first to push
for increasing protections

00:30:47.550 --> 00:30:50.400
to those most at risk,
particularly the elderly.

00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:52.230
Almost a year ago,
I recognized we

00:30:52.230 --> 00:30:55.240
must consider the enormous
harms to physical health,

00:30:55.240 --> 00:30:58.170
mental health, and lives
lost coming directly

00:30:58.170 --> 00:31:00.930
from the draconian
policies that attempted

00:31:00.930 --> 00:31:02.730
to contain the infection.

00:31:02.730 --> 00:31:04.680
That is the most
appropriate goal

00:31:04.680 --> 00:31:08.820
of people in public health
policy, to minimize all harms,

00:31:08.820 --> 00:31:13.280
not simply to stop
COVID-19 at all costs.

00:31:13.280 --> 00:31:18.180
[APPLAUSE]

00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:21.570
The claim in a recent Journal
of the AMA opinion piece,

00:31:21.570 --> 00:31:26.530
a vicious piece written by three
Stanford professors, that said,

00:31:26.530 --> 00:31:30.210
quote, nearly all public
health experts were concerned

00:31:30.210 --> 00:31:33.660
that Atlas' recommendations
could lead to tens of thousands

00:31:33.660 --> 00:31:36.750
of unnecessary deaths in
the United States alone,

00:31:36.750 --> 00:31:41.820
unquote, is patently
false, absurd on its face.

00:31:41.820 --> 00:31:44.550
As Professor Arnn
mentioned, the proposal

00:31:44.550 --> 00:31:47.610
called the Great Barrington
Declaration, co-authored

00:31:47.610 --> 00:31:49.800
by some of the world's
best medical scientists

00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:52.920
and epidemiologists from
Stanford, Harvard, and Oxford,

00:31:52.920 --> 00:31:56.730
is, quote, far closer to the one
condemned in the JAMA article

00:31:56.730 --> 00:31:58.740
than anything Atlas
said, unquote,

00:31:58.740 --> 00:32:00.570
as pointed out by Zinberg.

00:32:00.570 --> 00:32:02.910
Yet that policy
document has already

00:32:02.910 --> 00:32:06.150
been signed by over 50,000
medical and public health

00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:07.620
practitioners.

00:32:07.620 --> 00:32:09.810
When critics display
such ignorance

00:32:09.810 --> 00:32:12.690
about the scope of
views held by experts,

00:32:12.690 --> 00:32:16.320
it exposes their overt bias
and wholly disqualifies

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:18.540
their authority on these issues.

00:32:18.540 --> 00:32:21.180
Indeed, it is
almost beyond parody

00:32:21.180 --> 00:32:23.620
that these same
Stanford critics wrote,

00:32:23.620 --> 00:32:26.910
quote, professionalism demands
honesty about what they

00:32:26.910 --> 00:32:28.575
know and do not know, unquote.

00:32:31.470 --> 00:32:33.510
It is true that I have
explained the fact

00:32:33.510 --> 00:32:36.270
that younger people have little
risk from this infection,

00:32:36.270 --> 00:32:39.210
as well as the biological
concept of herd

00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:41.520
immunity, the most
radioactive term

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:44.910
in the pandemic discussion.

00:32:44.910 --> 00:32:48.690
That explanation is very
different from proposing

00:32:48.690 --> 00:32:51.750
that people be deliberately
exposed and infected.

00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:53.520
I have never done that.

00:32:53.520 --> 00:32:55.440
To the contrary,
I have repeatedly

00:32:55.440 --> 00:32:57.690
called for mitigation
measures, including

00:32:57.690 --> 00:33:01.320
extra sanitization,
social distancing, masks

00:33:01.320 --> 00:33:03.600
when appropriate,
group limits, testing,

00:33:03.600 --> 00:33:06.210
and other increased
protections to limit the spread

00:33:06.210 --> 00:33:08.530
and the damage from the virus.

00:33:08.530 --> 00:33:12.420
I explicitly call for augmenting
protection of those at risk

00:33:12.420 --> 00:33:15.810
in dozens of on the
record presentations,

00:33:15.810 --> 00:33:18.540
interviews, and written pieces.

00:33:18.540 --> 00:33:22.380
Yet one must question
why these accusers ignore

00:33:22.380 --> 00:33:26.040
these explicit
emphatic denials of me,

00:33:26.040 --> 00:33:29.070
beyond those
presentations, that I ever

00:33:29.070 --> 00:33:32.760
supported spreading the
infection unchecked to achieve

00:33:32.760 --> 00:33:33.990
herd immunity.

00:33:33.990 --> 00:33:36.960
These denials were quoted
widely in the media.

00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:39.270
Are not my own
statements the object

00:33:39.270 --> 00:33:41.250
of their criticism
in the first place?

00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:43.080
Or might it be something else?

00:33:43.080 --> 00:33:45.780
Might it be due to these
Stanford professor's

00:33:45.780 --> 00:33:48.450
own political rage,
their own desire

00:33:48.450 --> 00:33:52.020
to delegitimize anyone
who had the audacity

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:55.280
to help the country
under President Trump.

00:33:55.280 --> 00:33:58.220
[APPLAUSE]

00:34:02.640 --> 00:34:05.190
For many months, I was
vilified after calling

00:34:05.190 --> 00:34:08.850
for opening in-person
schools, the same exact policy

00:34:08.850 --> 00:34:11.350
that Harvard professors
Martin Kulldorf and Katherine

00:34:11.350 --> 00:34:14.070
Yee and Stanford professor,
and my good friend, Jay

00:34:14.070 --> 00:34:16.320
Bhattacharya called for.

00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:18.750
But this policy has
been corroborated,

00:34:18.750 --> 00:34:22.710
upheld with all the evidence
repeatedly for months.

00:34:22.710 --> 00:34:24.900
The compelling case
to open schools

00:34:24.900 --> 00:34:27.810
is admitted to be long
standing truth now,

00:34:27.810 --> 00:34:31.110
even in lay publications
like The Atlantic.

00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:33.659
They said, quote, research
from around the world

00:34:33.659 --> 00:34:36.690
has, since the beginning
of the pandemic,

00:34:36.690 --> 00:34:39.960
indicated that people under
18 and especially younger kids

00:34:39.960 --> 00:34:42.030
are less susceptible
to infection,

00:34:42.030 --> 00:34:44.400
less likely to experience
severe symptoms,

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:47.460
and far less likely to be
hospitalized or die, unquote.

00:34:47.460 --> 00:34:49.739
And quote, we've
known for months

00:34:49.739 --> 00:34:52.170
that young children
are less susceptible

00:34:52.170 --> 00:34:55.139
to serious infection and less
likely to transmit the virus.

00:34:55.139 --> 00:34:59.100
Let's act like it, unquote.

00:34:59.100 --> 00:35:03.300
The JAMA accusers further
stated, Atlas disputed the need

00:35:03.300 --> 00:35:05.700
for masks, unquote.

00:35:05.700 --> 00:35:07.800
Talk about radioactive issues.

00:35:07.800 --> 00:35:09.060
Let's talk about masks.

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:16.320
To the contrary, my advice
on mask usage was consistent.

00:35:16.320 --> 00:35:19.500
And I said it more
than 100 times.

00:35:19.500 --> 00:35:22.740
Wear a mask when you cannot
socially distance, quote,

00:35:22.740 --> 00:35:23.850
unquote.

00:35:23.850 --> 00:35:28.830
What's funny is that that
matches almost verbatim

00:35:28.830 --> 00:35:32.220
the published recommendations of
the World Health Organization.

00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:36.060
Quote, when outside, wear a mask
if you cannot maintain physical

00:35:36.060 --> 00:35:38.850
distance from others, unquote.

00:35:38.850 --> 00:35:42.090
And in December, they changed
it to, quote, in areas where

00:35:42.090 --> 00:35:45.090
the virus is circulating, masks
should be worn when you're

00:35:45.090 --> 00:35:47.400
in crowded settings,
when you can't

00:35:47.400 --> 00:35:50.820
be one meter from
others, and in rooms

00:35:50.820 --> 00:35:54.180
with poor or unknown
ventilation, unquote, i.e.

00:35:54.180 --> 00:35:57.900
not at all times by everyone.

00:35:57.900 --> 00:36:01.350
That also matches the NIH.

00:36:01.350 --> 00:36:05.670
Quote, when consistent
distancing is not possible,

00:36:05.670 --> 00:36:08.970
face coverings may
further reduce the spread

00:36:08.970 --> 00:36:13.320
of infectious droplets from
individuals with SARS2 COVID

00:36:13.320 --> 00:36:15.930
infection to others, unquote.

00:36:15.930 --> 00:36:20.220
You'll never hear that on CNN.

00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:21.750
You may not watch CNN.

00:36:21.750 --> 00:36:23.658
[LAUGHTER]

00:36:23.658 --> 00:36:26.043
[APPLAUSE]

00:36:29.870 --> 00:36:32.270
Let's talk about
universal mask usage

00:36:32.270 --> 00:36:34.160
in the general population.

00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:37.580
38 states have implemented
mask mandates, most

00:36:37.580 --> 00:36:40.190
since at least the summer with
almost all the rest having

00:36:40.190 --> 00:36:42.560
major city mask mandates.

00:36:42.560 --> 00:36:46.130
Widespread general
population mask usage

00:36:46.130 --> 00:36:48.920
has shown little
empirical utility

00:36:48.920 --> 00:36:52.580
for stopping cases all
over the world, every state

00:36:52.580 --> 00:36:56.030
in the country, even though
describing that evidence

00:36:56.030 --> 00:36:58.010
has been censored.

00:36:58.010 --> 00:37:01.550
Widespread mass usage
shows only minimal impact

00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:05.750
in the one large randomized
controlled study from Denmark.

00:37:05.750 --> 00:37:07.110
Here's the reality.

00:37:07.110 --> 00:37:10.460
Those who insist that universal
mask usage is absolutely

00:37:10.460 --> 00:37:14.030
proven effective at controlling
the spread of this virus

00:37:14.030 --> 00:37:18.710
and somehow is universally
recommended by the science

00:37:18.710 --> 00:37:22.280
are deliberately ignoring
the evidence to the contrary.

00:37:22.280 --> 00:37:26.573
And they are propagating false
and misleading information.

00:37:26.573 --> 00:37:32.260
[APPLAUSE]

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:35.470
Those who charge that it
is unethical or dangerous

00:37:35.470 --> 00:37:38.590
to question broad
population mask mandates

00:37:38.590 --> 00:37:42.790
must explain why several of the
world's top infectious disease

00:37:42.790 --> 00:37:46.450
scientists and public
health organizations overtly

00:37:46.450 --> 00:37:49.780
questioned the efficacy of
general population mask.

00:37:49.780 --> 00:37:52.060
Jefferson and Heneghan
of Oxford Center

00:37:52.060 --> 00:37:53.870
for Evidence-Based
Medicine wrote,

00:37:53.870 --> 00:37:56.230
quote, it would appear
that, despite two

00:37:56.230 --> 00:37:58.450
decades of pandemic
preparedness,

00:37:58.450 --> 00:38:01.000
there is considerable
uncertainty as to value

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:03.010
of wearing masks, unquote.

00:38:03.010 --> 00:38:06.280
Oxford's Sunetra Gupta said,
there is no need for masks

00:38:06.280 --> 00:38:08.710
unless one is
elderly or high risk.

00:38:08.710 --> 00:38:12.670
Stanford's Jay Bhattacharya
stated, quote, mask mandates

00:38:12.670 --> 00:38:15.070
are not supported by
the scientific data.

00:38:15.070 --> 00:38:18.430
There is no scientific
evidence that mask mandates

00:38:18.430 --> 00:38:21.250
work to slow the spread
of the disease, unquote.

00:38:21.250 --> 00:38:23.710
Throughout the
pandemic, the WHO said,

00:38:23.710 --> 00:38:26.470
at present, there is
no direct evidence

00:38:26.470 --> 00:38:28.690
on the effectiveness
of universal masking

00:38:28.690 --> 00:38:31.870
of healthy people in the
community to prevent infection

00:38:31.870 --> 00:38:36.220
with respiratory viruses,
including COVID-19, unquote.

00:38:36.220 --> 00:38:40.660
The CDC reviewed influenza
pandemics and published in May.

00:38:40.660 --> 00:38:43.090
Quote, they did
not find evidence

00:38:43.090 --> 00:38:45.070
that surgical type
face masks are

00:38:45.070 --> 00:38:48.670
effective in reducing
laboratory confirmed influenza

00:38:48.670 --> 00:38:51.730
transmission, either when
worn by infected persons

00:38:51.730 --> 00:38:55.390
source control or by persons in
the general community to reduce

00:38:55.390 --> 00:38:58.240
their susceptibility, unquote.

00:38:58.240 --> 00:39:01.510
And until the WHO
removed the quote

00:39:01.510 --> 00:39:07.840
that I used of theirs in my
tweet, that was withdrawn

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:10.360
and censored by
Twitter, they had

00:39:10.360 --> 00:39:15.280
posted, until the very next
day, quote, at the present time,

00:39:15.280 --> 00:39:18.370
the widespread use of masks by
healthy people in the community

00:39:18.370 --> 00:39:21.400
setting is not yet
supported by high quality

00:39:21.400 --> 00:39:23.140
or direct scientific evidence.

00:39:23.140 --> 00:39:29.220
And there are potential benefits
and harms to consider, period.

00:39:29.220 --> 00:39:33.180
At this point, one
could make a strong case

00:39:33.180 --> 00:39:36.810
that those who continue to
push societal restrictions

00:39:36.810 --> 00:39:39.750
without acknowledging their
failures and serious harms

00:39:39.750 --> 00:39:45.270
are themselves putting forth
dangerous misinformation.

00:39:45.270 --> 00:39:49.590
But I will not call for their
official rebuke or punishment.

00:39:49.590 --> 00:39:51.450
I will not try to cancel them.

00:39:51.450 --> 00:39:54.280
I will not try to
extinguish their opinions.

00:39:54.280 --> 00:39:58.860
And I will not lie to distort
their words and defame them.

00:39:58.860 --> 00:40:02.130
To do so would repeat
their shameful behavior

00:40:02.130 --> 00:40:03.990
of intimidating
discourse that is

00:40:03.990 --> 00:40:06.900
critical to educating
the public and arriving

00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:10.750
at the scientific truth
we desperately need.

00:40:10.750 --> 00:40:14.790
It's time to consider
that university models,

00:40:14.790 --> 00:40:18.540
like Harvard's truth, Stanford's
the winds of freedom blow,

00:40:18.540 --> 00:40:22.590
and Yale's light and
truth need major revision.

00:40:22.590 --> 00:40:25.560
Social media has piled
on with a heavy hand

00:40:25.560 --> 00:40:29.490
now to eliminate discussion
of conflicting evidence.

00:40:29.490 --> 00:40:32.520
Without permitting,
without indeed encouraging,

00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:35.850
open debate and
admission of errors,

00:40:35.850 --> 00:40:39.340
we might never solve
any future crisis.

00:40:39.340 --> 00:40:44.640
As a health policy
scholar for over 15 years

00:40:44.640 --> 00:40:48.000
and as a professor at top
universities for 30 years,

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:50.790
I am shocked at what I see.

00:40:50.790 --> 00:40:53.880
Some faculty members of
our acclaimed universities

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:57.600
are now dangerously
intolerant, dangerously

00:40:57.600 --> 00:41:01.817
intolerant of opinions
that they don't agree with.

00:41:01.817 --> 00:41:03.685
[APPLAUSE]

00:41:07.900 --> 00:41:11.800
Some go even further,
distorting and misrepresenting

00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:15.910
words to delegitimize and
even calling for punishment

00:41:15.910 --> 00:41:18.820
of those of us willing
to serve the country

00:41:18.820 --> 00:41:23.710
alongside a polarizing president
that they happen to loathe.

00:41:23.710 --> 00:41:27.700
It is their behavior to quote
those same professors rebuking

00:41:27.700 --> 00:41:32.260
me that, quote, violates the
core values of Stanford faculty

00:41:32.260 --> 00:41:35.410
and the expectations under
the Stanford code of conduct,

00:41:35.410 --> 00:41:39.250
which states, quote, we are
all responsible for sustaining

00:41:39.250 --> 00:41:43.630
the high ethical standards
of this institution, unquote.

00:41:43.630 --> 00:41:46.600
But worse than that
violation of ethical behavior

00:41:46.600 --> 00:41:49.330
among colleagues,
their behavior does not

00:41:49.330 --> 00:41:53.620
meet the standard of
simple human decency.

00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:57.790
If academic leaders, if the
entire academic community

00:41:57.790 --> 00:42:01.930
fails to stand up and renounce
that unethical conduct,

00:42:01.930 --> 00:42:04.870
many more experts with
a reputation to lose

00:42:04.870 --> 00:42:08.530
will be unwilling to serve their
country in contentious times.

00:42:08.530 --> 00:42:11.650
As educators, as parents,
as fellow citizens,

00:42:11.650 --> 00:42:13.990
that would be the
worst possible legacy

00:42:13.990 --> 00:42:16.630
to leave to our children.

00:42:16.630 --> 00:42:20.650
I also fear that the
concept the science

00:42:20.650 --> 00:42:23.046
has been seriously damaged.

00:42:23.046 --> 00:42:27.810
[APPLAUSE]

00:42:27.810 --> 00:42:30.720
Even the best journals in the
world, New England Journal

00:42:30.720 --> 00:42:35.090
of Medicine, Lancet, Science,
Nature, and Journal of the AMA

00:42:35.090 --> 00:42:39.430
have become overtly
contaminated by politics.

00:42:39.430 --> 00:42:42.030
Many, unfortunately,
have now become

00:42:42.030 --> 00:42:44.910
fatigued by these arguments.

00:42:44.910 --> 00:42:46.680
That is even worse.

00:42:46.680 --> 00:42:49.290
Because if the public
becomes fatigued,

00:42:49.290 --> 00:42:54.170
that will allow a fallacy
to triumph over truth.

00:42:54.170 --> 00:42:56.270
If the social media
continues to be

00:42:56.270 --> 00:42:59.030
the arbiter of
allowable discussion,

00:42:59.030 --> 00:43:00.890
the United States
is on the precipice

00:43:00.890 --> 00:43:03.500
of losing its
cherished freedoms,

00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:05.960
with censorship and
cancellation of all those

00:43:05.960 --> 00:43:08.420
who bring views forward that
differ from the accepted

00:43:08.420 --> 00:43:10.830
mainstream.

00:43:10.830 --> 00:43:14.340
I stand here
honestly more renewed

00:43:14.340 --> 00:43:16.380
than I was when I
walked in this building,

00:43:16.380 --> 00:43:19.370
because I have never seen
Hillsdale College before.

00:43:19.370 --> 00:43:21.765
[APPLAUSE]

00:43:30.880 --> 00:43:33.610
I will say this in conclusion.

00:43:33.610 --> 00:43:36.910
While it is not clear if
our democracy will survive,

00:43:36.910 --> 00:43:42.340
it is obvious that people must
step up, and I may say rise up,

00:43:42.340 --> 00:43:44.050
or it has no chance.

00:43:44.050 --> 00:43:45.546
Thank you very much.

00:43:45.546 --> 00:43:48.402
[APPLAUSE]

00:43:50.310 --> 00:43:51.248
Thank you.

00:43:51.248 --> 00:43:53.688
[CHEERING]

00:43:55.640 --> 00:43:56.616
Thank you very much.

00:43:56.616 --> 00:44:01.008
[CHEERING]

00:44:01.008 --> 00:44:01.984
Thank you.

00:44:01.984 --> 00:44:04.912
[APPLAUSE]

00:44:09.330 --> 00:44:10.686
Thank you very much.

00:44:10.686 --> 00:44:16.040
[APPLAUSE]

00:44:16.040 --> 00:44:17.450
SPEAKER 2: Thank you, Dr. Atlas.

00:44:17.450 --> 00:44:20.400
We now have time for some
Q&amp;A. If you have a question,

00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:22.580
please raise your hand
and wait for a microphone

00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:23.455
to be brought to you.

00:44:47.120 --> 00:44:47.620
Sir.

00:44:50.810 --> 00:44:54.140
AUDIENCE: I am 75
years old and sort

00:44:54.140 --> 00:44:55.760
of on the horns of a dilemma.

00:44:55.760 --> 00:44:59.880
And that dilemma is whether
or not to get the vaccination.

00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:02.870
So what's your opinion
of what we should

00:45:02.870 --> 00:45:05.503
do under these circumstances.

00:45:05.503 --> 00:45:06.170
SCOTT ATLAS: OK.

00:45:06.170 --> 00:45:07.730
This is a common
question actually

00:45:07.730 --> 00:45:11.270
tonight before the dinner.

00:45:11.270 --> 00:45:14.120
So I mean, I'll first say,
I'm not anybody's doctor here.

00:45:14.120 --> 00:45:16.055
And you should consult
with your doctor.

00:45:19.430 --> 00:45:22.100
I can say this, and this
is what I tell people.

00:45:22.100 --> 00:45:25.580
I think, and I've said it on
the podium in the press briefing

00:45:25.580 --> 00:45:30.050
room, so I feel that
people who are at risk

00:45:30.050 --> 00:45:32.630
should get the vaccine.

00:45:32.630 --> 00:45:35.510
And what I mean by that
is, besides the people

00:45:35.510 --> 00:45:38.450
who have high risk conditions,
people who are generally

00:45:38.450 --> 00:45:43.050
over roughly 65, it's
advisable to get the vaccine.

00:45:43.050 --> 00:45:45.660
And I say that for two reasons.

00:45:45.660 --> 00:45:48.890
One is that the
risk of the vaccine

00:45:48.890 --> 00:45:53.030
is smaller than the
risk from COVID-19

00:45:53.030 --> 00:45:55.040
for people who are old.

00:45:55.040 --> 00:45:56.810
I consider myself--

00:45:56.810 --> 00:45:59.160
I don't consider myself old,
but I did get the vaccine

00:45:59.160 --> 00:46:02.300
two days ago.

00:46:02.300 --> 00:46:05.360
And the second reason is
sort of a secondary reason,

00:46:05.360 --> 00:46:08.090
but it's the reality of
the country we're living

00:46:08.090 --> 00:46:10.700
and the world we're living in.

00:46:10.700 --> 00:46:14.010
I believe, I don't
want it to be true.

00:46:14.010 --> 00:46:16.550
But I believe that
we're probably

00:46:16.550 --> 00:46:18.590
going to be required
to show that we

00:46:18.590 --> 00:46:23.240
had the vaccine before we're
allowed to do certain things.

00:46:23.240 --> 00:46:24.620
I actually believe that.

00:46:24.620 --> 00:46:26.120
It's sad.

00:46:26.120 --> 00:46:27.830
But this is the world
we're looking at.

00:46:27.830 --> 00:46:29.480
And what I'm talking
about specifically

00:46:29.480 --> 00:46:31.190
is things like
international travel.

00:46:31.190 --> 00:46:34.100
I believe-- I have no
inside knowledge on this.

00:46:34.100 --> 00:46:37.970
I'm not in the
discussion at all--

00:46:37.970 --> 00:46:42.270
that countries could easily
start requiring that.

00:46:42.270 --> 00:46:45.990
And I do travel quite a bit.

00:46:45.990 --> 00:46:50.030
So those two things in
the right age group,

00:46:50.030 --> 00:46:51.930
I think it's advisable
to get the vaccine.

00:46:51.930 --> 00:46:54.740
And I think it probably will
be required, although I have

00:46:54.740 --> 00:46:56.540
no inside knowledge on that.

00:46:56.540 --> 00:46:59.930
If you're asking me, should
everyone get the vaccine?

00:46:59.930 --> 00:47:03.920
Again, I'm going to say it's
a personal decision with you

00:47:03.920 --> 00:47:06.050
and your doctor.

00:47:06.050 --> 00:47:08.720
I do not believe,
for one second,

00:47:08.720 --> 00:47:11.480
that people should be
required to get a vaccine.

00:47:11.480 --> 00:47:14.290
No, I am completely
opposed to that.

00:47:14.290 --> 00:47:20.290
[APPLAUSE]

00:47:20.290 --> 00:47:25.390
If you're low risk and young,
I think there's a strong case

00:47:25.390 --> 00:47:27.310
to not take the vaccine.

00:47:27.310 --> 00:47:29.750
I have two children of
my own in that age group.

00:47:29.750 --> 00:47:32.050
And I've advised
them accordingly.

00:47:32.050 --> 00:47:36.220
But again, like it's
a personal decision.

00:47:36.220 --> 00:47:37.300
There are certain risks.

00:47:37.300 --> 00:47:40.780
I would say this, if I
can go on a little bit.

00:47:40.780 --> 00:47:44.650
I was there, from what
I saw and what I know,

00:47:44.650 --> 00:47:48.890
there were no corners cut
on the vaccine development.

00:47:48.890 --> 00:47:51.430
In fact, there were
extra delays put

00:47:51.430 --> 00:47:57.130
in against standards to
delay the emergency use

00:47:57.130 --> 00:47:58.450
authorization.

00:47:58.450 --> 00:48:04.030
So I do not believe at all that
the vaccines were somehow short

00:48:04.030 --> 00:48:06.730
circuiting safety measures.

00:48:06.730 --> 00:48:10.030
I disagree with that.

00:48:10.030 --> 00:48:12.310
There is a certain
percentage of complications

00:48:12.310 --> 00:48:14.590
from any time you're going
to inject into your body

00:48:14.590 --> 00:48:15.160
something.

00:48:15.160 --> 00:48:15.820
That's clear.

00:48:15.820 --> 00:48:18.340
And vaccines are
in that category.

00:48:18.340 --> 00:48:20.950
But it's a cost
benefit or a risk

00:48:20.950 --> 00:48:26.740
ben-- a risk sort of benefit
assessment for an individual.

00:48:26.740 --> 00:48:28.832
SPEAKER 2: We have a--

00:48:28.832 --> 00:48:30.540
We have a question on
the speaker's left.

00:48:34.690 --> 00:48:36.820
AUDIENCE: Dr. Atlas,
I just recently read,

00:48:36.820 --> 00:48:38.590
and I can't say who quoted it.

00:48:38.590 --> 00:48:40.360
But it was a quote
that saying that those

00:48:40.360 --> 00:48:43.390
who had the coronavirus
and then who recovered

00:48:43.390 --> 00:48:49.750
should only get the first
shot of the inoculation.

00:48:49.750 --> 00:48:52.930
And I thought, presumably,
if you've had the disease,

00:48:52.930 --> 00:48:53.980
you have the antibodies.

00:48:53.980 --> 00:48:56.170
You have the memory
cells in your blood.

00:48:56.170 --> 00:48:58.900
What the heck is that about that
they should get the first shot?

00:48:58.900 --> 00:49:00.010
Do you have an opinion on that?

00:49:00.010 --> 00:49:00.550
Have you heard that?

00:49:00.550 --> 00:49:01.758
I can't remember who said it.

00:49:01.758 --> 00:49:02.860
SCOTT ATLAS: Yes.

00:49:02.860 --> 00:49:05.810
So I mean, there's two parts to
that really that are important.

00:49:05.810 --> 00:49:09.170
One is, when you're talking
about prioritizing vaccines,

00:49:09.170 --> 00:49:13.570
this is one of the things
that is, again, like this is--

00:49:13.570 --> 00:49:17.020
I've said on TV I feel like I'm
living in a Kafka novel here.

00:49:17.020 --> 00:49:19.630
I mean, there's
never been anyone

00:49:19.630 --> 00:49:23.410
that says, in the administration
or in the people that

00:49:23.410 --> 00:49:25.750
are in charge
nowadays, that says

00:49:25.750 --> 00:49:28.570
that you should not
be a priority if you

00:49:28.570 --> 00:49:30.940
had the infection.

00:49:30.940 --> 00:49:32.890
And of course, you
should not be a priority.

00:49:32.890 --> 00:49:34.932
I'm not saying you should
never take the vaccine.

00:49:34.932 --> 00:49:37.360
But you don't need
it right away.

00:49:37.360 --> 00:49:41.750
You should immunize the people
who have a high risk to die.

00:49:41.750 --> 00:49:45.790
And if you've had the infection,
you have biological protection.

00:49:45.790 --> 00:49:47.290
That's just-- that's fact.

00:49:47.290 --> 00:49:49.660
That's high school AP biology.

00:49:49.660 --> 00:49:51.670
That's not even medical school.

00:49:51.670 --> 00:49:53.320
And that's what
the research shows.

00:49:53.320 --> 00:49:57.070
But somehow, that's
just not discussed.

00:49:57.070 --> 00:49:59.530
The second part of
your question is,

00:49:59.530 --> 00:50:04.840
there is some evidence
that people that

00:50:04.840 --> 00:50:09.070
have had the infection, when
they get the first dose,

00:50:09.070 --> 00:50:12.820
they have the same immune
response to the first dose,

00:50:12.820 --> 00:50:17.830
quantitatively, as a regular
person without the infection

00:50:17.830 --> 00:50:19.260
who had both doses.

00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:20.960
That's where that's coming from.

00:50:20.960 --> 00:50:26.770
So if you have the X immune
response after two doses

00:50:26.770 --> 00:50:28.285
and you've never
had the infection,

00:50:28.285 --> 00:50:30.160
if you take somebody
who's had the infection,

00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:33.110
gets the first dose, they
also have X immune response.

00:50:33.110 --> 00:50:35.590
So they are sort
of fully protected

00:50:35.590 --> 00:50:36.792
or equivalently protected.

00:50:36.792 --> 00:50:38.000
That's where that comes from.

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:41.080
I don't have an opinion
on how that will be.

00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:42.640
But I do have an
opinion that people

00:50:42.640 --> 00:50:44.200
who have had the
infection should not

00:50:44.200 --> 00:50:47.510
be the first priority
to get vaccinated.

00:50:47.510 --> 00:50:50.960
We should vaccinate the people
who are at high risk to die.

00:50:50.960 --> 00:50:53.920
That's the only
reason to do vaccines

00:50:53.920 --> 00:50:55.450
is to stop people from dying.

00:51:02.313 --> 00:51:02.980
AUDIENCE: Hello.

00:51:02.980 --> 00:51:04.828
SCOTT ATLAS: Hi.

00:51:04.828 --> 00:51:06.620
AUDIENCE: I want to
first congratulate you.

00:51:06.620 --> 00:51:09.663
It was a wonderful speech,
and it had a lot to say.

00:51:09.663 --> 00:51:10.410
[APPLAUSE]

00:51:10.410 --> 00:51:13.025
SCOTT ATLAS: Thank
you very much.

00:51:13.025 --> 00:51:14.400
AUDIENCE: Secondly,
is this going

00:51:14.400 --> 00:51:16.350
to be available to
us in a written form

00:51:16.350 --> 00:51:19.770
that we're allowed to ask for?

00:51:19.770 --> 00:51:22.170
SCOTT ATLAS: I think
it's going to be--

00:51:22.170 --> 00:51:25.890
it's on the internet if I'm
not mistaken, number one.

00:51:25.890 --> 00:51:29.670
Number two, much
of this I'm going

00:51:29.670 --> 00:51:36.120
to submit as a written
piece to one of the--

00:51:36.120 --> 00:51:38.730
one of the Stanford newspapers.

00:51:38.730 --> 00:51:42.330
Because I'm really tired
of what's going on.

00:51:42.330 --> 00:51:43.840
And I'm not going to take it.

00:51:43.840 --> 00:51:45.187
I'm not going to take it.

00:51:45.187 --> 00:51:48.169
[APPLAUSE]

00:51:54.630 --> 00:51:58.620
AUDIENCE: Dr. Atlas,
I'll be 85 in May.

00:51:58.620 --> 00:52:00.960
And I've been inoculated,
so I'm ready to go.

00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:06.630
But all summer long,
I've turned on the TV.

00:52:06.630 --> 00:52:11.550
And I saw Dr. Fauci and
Dr. Scarf telling us what

00:52:11.550 --> 00:52:13.800
the science was in the moment.

00:52:13.800 --> 00:52:17.280
And I was wondering if you
could elaborate a little bit as

00:52:17.280 --> 00:52:21.795
to how much of that was science,
how much of that was politics.

00:52:25.530 --> 00:52:32.110
SCOTT ATLAS: Well, no, I have no
hesitancy in telling the truth.

00:52:32.110 --> 00:52:33.960
I'll tell you it this way first.

00:52:33.960 --> 00:52:35.320
I wasn't there.

00:52:35.320 --> 00:52:41.420
You have to remember, I didn't
come in until mid-August.

00:52:41.420 --> 00:52:44.240
So a lot of stuff was said.

00:52:44.240 --> 00:52:45.680
And then nothing was said.

00:52:45.680 --> 00:52:48.050
Because then the president
discontinued these press

00:52:48.050 --> 00:52:51.040
conferences.

00:52:51.040 --> 00:52:55.700
What I saw inside
the White House,

00:52:55.700 --> 00:52:58.790
inside the what's called the
situation room where the task

00:52:58.790 --> 00:53:03.510
force meets, is incredible.

00:53:03.510 --> 00:53:04.940
It's shocking.

00:53:04.940 --> 00:53:08.930
It's outrageous what was said.

00:53:08.930 --> 00:53:13.610
And I'm going to have
to write about that one,

00:53:13.610 --> 00:53:15.650
because it's amazing.

00:53:15.650 --> 00:53:17.780
But it's sort of
frightening the level

00:53:17.780 --> 00:53:22.490
of knowledge, the lack of
knowledge of the current data.

00:53:26.200 --> 00:53:30.930
And I think the answer really,
it can be summed up as this.

00:53:30.930 --> 00:53:34.060
These are people who are
government bureaucrats.

00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:37.150
These are people who have worked
in government jobs for 30,

00:53:37.150 --> 00:53:39.950
40 years.

00:53:39.950 --> 00:53:44.060
These are not people who are
challenged intellectually

00:53:44.060 --> 00:53:47.360
by other people who come in
and say, well, what about this?

00:53:47.360 --> 00:53:51.500
People like me, and they bring
in a dozen scientific papers

00:53:51.500 --> 00:53:52.880
and go through the data.

00:53:52.880 --> 00:53:55.560
That didn't happen
before I got there.

00:53:55.560 --> 00:54:01.310
And when you have
people who are talking,

00:54:01.310 --> 00:54:05.720
like they're talking now
on TV, about, well, we

00:54:05.720 --> 00:54:07.760
should pass this
bill or something

00:54:07.760 --> 00:54:10.478
like this, that's not science.

00:54:10.478 --> 00:54:11.145
That's politics.

00:54:13.790 --> 00:54:18.560
So I think, it's tough
to say the truth.

00:54:18.560 --> 00:54:20.300
It's actually easy
to say the truth.

00:54:20.300 --> 00:54:25.550
It's tough to watch people
lie about what you said.

00:54:25.550 --> 00:54:28.940
But a lot of things
that were said

00:54:28.940 --> 00:54:32.060
were sort of difficult to--

00:54:32.060 --> 00:54:33.480
difficult to
believe, I will say.

00:54:33.480 --> 00:54:34.700
I'll leave it at that.

00:54:44.200 --> 00:54:45.950
LARRY ARNN: To the man
who asked if you're

00:54:45.950 --> 00:54:49.010
going to get to read
this, the answer is yes.

00:54:49.010 --> 00:54:49.896
SCOTT ATLAS: OK.

00:54:49.896 --> 00:54:54.175
[APPLAUSE]

00:54:54.175 --> 00:54:56.550
SPEAKER 2: We have a question
on the speaker's left-- oh,

00:54:56.550 --> 00:54:59.718
I apologize.

00:54:59.718 --> 00:55:02.010
AUDIENCE: Thank you very much
for your remarks tonight.

00:55:02.010 --> 00:55:02.940
They were tremendous.

00:55:02.940 --> 00:55:06.782
And more so, thank you for your
action in serving our country.

00:55:06.782 --> 00:55:07.740
SCOTT ATLAS: Thank you.

00:55:07.740 --> 00:55:09.198
AUDIENCE: My
question, you referred

00:55:09.198 --> 00:55:12.510
to the incredible power
asserted by our government

00:55:12.510 --> 00:55:18.270
to shut down the largest economy
known in the history of mankind

00:55:18.270 --> 00:55:21.480
without having set
a goal or a purpose.

00:55:21.480 --> 00:55:26.550
I recall early on that there was
a goal of flattening the curve,

00:55:26.550 --> 00:55:30.450
and not necessarily
completely destroying

00:55:30.450 --> 00:55:32.820
the virus for all
time but trying

00:55:32.820 --> 00:55:37.560
to get the infection rate
to be below the capacities

00:55:37.560 --> 00:55:39.910
for emergency rooms, et cetera.

00:55:39.910 --> 00:55:42.090
Whatever happened to that,
and what is the goal?

00:55:45.330 --> 00:55:47.520
SCOTT ATLAS: I find myself
asking that frequently.

00:55:47.520 --> 00:55:48.990
[LAUGHTER]

00:55:48.990 --> 00:55:49.650
You're right.

00:55:49.650 --> 00:55:55.140
And I remember, back in the
spring or whenever that was,

00:55:55.140 --> 00:55:58.350
the press conference that was a
very good press conference when

00:55:58.350 --> 00:55:59.910
Dr. Birx explained
that we're going

00:55:59.910 --> 00:56:03.600
to flatten the curve,
which only meant one thing.

00:56:03.600 --> 00:56:09.060
The hospitalizations they didn't
want to have exceed capacity.

00:56:09.060 --> 00:56:12.060
It had nothing to do with
stopping people from dying.

00:56:12.060 --> 00:56:13.710
If people want to
talk mathematically,

00:56:13.710 --> 00:56:17.880
the area under the curve
was never changing.

00:56:17.880 --> 00:56:21.000
It was simply that they were
going to delay it so that, A,

00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:24.630
hospitals could treat people,
including, by the way,

00:56:24.630 --> 00:56:28.890
people without COVID,
which they failed to do.

00:56:28.890 --> 00:56:31.770
But that was voluntary
and fear induced.

00:56:31.770 --> 00:56:33.300
But the second
reason for the delay

00:56:33.300 --> 00:56:38.070
was at least there was some
time for mobilizing resources,

00:56:38.070 --> 00:56:41.670
ramping up production of
personal protective equipment,

00:56:41.670 --> 00:56:43.440
getting a head start
on drug development.

00:56:43.440 --> 00:56:48.000
These are all rational
reasons to temporarily,

00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:49.620
you know, close things.

00:56:49.620 --> 00:56:54.840
And you may or may not remember,
but President Trump very early

00:56:54.840 --> 00:57:00.540
on, and repeatedly, said we
cannot have the cure be worse

00:57:00.540 --> 00:57:02.830
than the disease.

00:57:02.830 --> 00:57:06.720
And there is something
so obvious and yet so

00:57:06.720 --> 00:57:08.160
wise about that.

00:57:08.160 --> 00:57:09.180
It's obvious.

00:57:09.180 --> 00:57:12.280
But nobody else was saying it.

00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:14.100
And that is what happened.

00:57:14.100 --> 00:57:16.260
So you're right
There has now been

00:57:16.260 --> 00:57:20.310
a complete transformation
of the goal to stopping

00:57:20.310 --> 00:57:24.030
all cases of COVID-19.

00:57:24.030 --> 00:57:27.760
And it's completely irrational.

00:57:27.760 --> 00:57:30.570
It has proven to be impossible.

00:57:30.570 --> 00:57:35.010
And it is so destructive
and harmful that it

00:57:35.010 --> 00:57:38.160
is one of the most egregious
failures of health care

00:57:38.160 --> 00:57:41.320
policy, really, in the
history of the modern world.

00:57:41.320 --> 00:57:43.696
I don't know how to
say it otherwise.

00:57:43.696 --> 00:57:47.960
[APPLAUSE]

00:57:47.960 --> 00:57:51.320
SPEAKER 2: We have a question
on the speaker's left.

00:57:51.320 --> 00:57:53.250
AUDIENCE: Hello, can
I ask you a question?

00:57:53.250 --> 00:57:57.560
Did you know that the
Arizona state legislature

00:57:57.560 --> 00:58:01.190
is in the process of
deciding whether people have

00:58:01.190 --> 00:58:05.330
to wear a mask totally,
or they can get away

00:58:05.330 --> 00:58:07.220
with not wearing a mask?

00:58:07.220 --> 00:58:09.830
And all they have to
do is get in touch

00:58:09.830 --> 00:58:13.010
with our state
representative and senators.

00:58:13.010 --> 00:58:18.710
And you can contact West
Valley Republican Office.

00:58:18.710 --> 00:58:21.530
Thank you.

00:58:21.530 --> 00:58:24.010
[APPLAUSE]

00:58:24.010 --> 00:58:25.504
SCOTT ATLAS: No, I didn't know.

00:58:25.504 --> 00:58:28.348
[LAUGHTER]

00:58:31.200 --> 00:58:31.700
Yes.

00:58:31.700 --> 00:58:32.533
AUDIENCE: Thank you.

00:58:32.533 --> 00:58:34.410
Good evening, thank
you for being here.

00:58:34.410 --> 00:58:38.070
Two part question, the first
is expressing a conundrum

00:58:38.070 --> 00:58:39.840
that I myself and
I think probably

00:58:39.840 --> 00:58:41.700
most of the people
in this room feel

00:58:41.700 --> 00:58:45.410
is a strong desire to rise up.

00:58:45.410 --> 00:58:49.970
We feel powerless to make a
difference in a world that

00:58:49.970 --> 00:58:51.500
is forcing compliance.

00:58:51.500 --> 00:58:53.660
If you want to shop
at HomeGoods, if you

00:58:53.660 --> 00:58:56.570
want to go to Home Depot, if
you want to go to the grocery

00:58:56.570 --> 00:58:59.960
store, if you want to live
your life, you must mask up.

00:58:59.960 --> 00:59:02.990
If you want to fly, if you want
to eat while you're flying,

00:59:02.990 --> 00:59:06.680
it's up and down with the mask.

00:59:06.680 --> 00:59:09.880
What is your advice
for those of us

00:59:09.880 --> 00:59:13.780
who choose to believe the
science, as you have described

00:59:13.780 --> 00:59:17.380
it, to rise up in a
way that is impactful

00:59:17.380 --> 00:59:21.910
and can change the way and
the course that we are facing?

00:59:21.910 --> 00:59:25.540
The second part, unrelated,
is around the power

00:59:25.540 --> 00:59:30.220
of local public health officials
to determine local public

00:59:30.220 --> 00:59:37.630
policy and health policy that
drive the local policies that

00:59:37.630 --> 00:59:40.850
are really impacting how
we're living our lives.

00:59:40.850 --> 00:59:42.343
Thank you.

00:59:42.343 --> 00:59:43.010
SCOTT ATLAS: OK.

00:59:43.010 --> 00:59:45.570
So the rise up
quote, by the way,

00:59:45.570 --> 00:59:48.120
means make your voices heard.

00:59:48.120 --> 00:59:51.170
I know that a lot of
people went insane

00:59:51.170 --> 00:59:53.420
when I said that on Twitter.

00:59:53.420 --> 00:59:56.150
Rise up means stand up,
make your voices heard.

00:59:56.150 --> 00:59:58.830
That's what a
democracy is all about.

00:59:58.830 --> 01:00:03.740
And so what I mean by how
you would do that is exactly

01:00:03.740 --> 01:00:08.960
that you must be aggressively
contacting, meaning be vocal,

01:00:08.960 --> 01:00:14.450
contact your representatives,
your local representatives.

01:00:14.450 --> 01:00:16.220
You have to basically--

01:00:16.220 --> 01:00:18.980
we have to make sure
that the people in charge

01:00:18.980 --> 01:00:22.850
are accountable to the people
who are in the population.

01:00:22.850 --> 01:00:26.030
And they're not accountable
if we just sit there.

01:00:26.030 --> 01:00:28.730
And so I speak to--

01:00:28.730 --> 01:00:31.850
I have spoken many times with
San Diego business community,

01:00:31.850 --> 01:00:33.590
as one example.

01:00:33.590 --> 01:00:36.110
And these guys,
these people, they

01:00:36.110 --> 01:00:37.940
want to open their businesses.

01:00:37.940 --> 01:00:40.670
And so they have their
city council members

01:00:40.670 --> 01:00:41.930
sit in on these meetings.

01:00:41.930 --> 01:00:44.970
They have their--
it's all about,

01:00:44.970 --> 01:00:49.100
we are the people in
charge, in theory.

01:00:49.100 --> 01:00:51.440
And so we have to really--

01:00:51.440 --> 01:00:52.820
we have to show it.

01:00:52.820 --> 01:00:55.760
It doesn't mean do something
destructive or violent

01:00:55.760 --> 01:00:56.700
or anything like that.

01:00:56.700 --> 01:00:59.750
That should be obvious to
any fair-minded person what

01:00:59.750 --> 01:01:00.500
we're saying here.

01:01:00.500 --> 01:01:05.040
But that means be on the
record, say what you want.

01:01:05.040 --> 01:01:07.730
I mean, the people of
California are rising up.

01:01:07.730 --> 01:01:10.375
There's a recall vote
going on with the governor.

01:01:10.375 --> 01:01:12.800
[APPLAUSE]

01:01:16.690 --> 01:01:19.270
Now the second part
of your question--

01:01:19.270 --> 01:01:21.580
there's no simple
answer to the question.

01:01:21.580 --> 01:01:23.320
There's no magic wand here.

01:01:23.320 --> 01:01:27.220
But it means actually
try to be impactful

01:01:27.220 --> 01:01:32.350
in your local communities
and get together as groups.

01:01:32.350 --> 01:01:35.590
Because I was saying earlier
that the individual person who

01:01:35.590 --> 01:01:39.640
owns the gym, who wants
to stand up and just open,

01:01:39.640 --> 01:01:41.410
OK, that person is squashed.

01:01:41.410 --> 01:01:44.230
And that just, it doesn't work.

01:01:44.230 --> 01:01:47.205
But it works if everybody opens.

01:01:47.205 --> 01:01:49.330
It works if all the
restaurants say, you know what?

01:01:49.330 --> 01:01:50.980
We're open.

01:01:50.980 --> 01:01:56.170
It works if the businesses say,
listen, we think we can open.

01:01:56.170 --> 01:01:58.480
If you don't want to
go to a restaurant,

01:01:58.480 --> 01:02:00.590
don't go as a customer.

01:02:00.590 --> 01:02:01.540
That's what I say.

01:02:01.540 --> 01:02:04.040
If you don't want to
go to a gym, don't go.

01:02:04.040 --> 01:02:06.620
[APPLAUSE]

01:02:06.620 --> 01:02:09.480
Now the second part is these
local public health officials,

01:02:09.480 --> 01:02:12.170
which is really incredible.

01:02:12.170 --> 01:02:14.760
This is, again, something
that we never knew.

01:02:14.760 --> 01:02:18.920
We never understood who had
this kind of power before.

01:02:18.920 --> 01:02:20.720
I live in Santa
Clara County, which

01:02:20.720 --> 01:02:23.930
is probably the most
restricted county

01:02:23.930 --> 01:02:25.410
in the state of California.

01:02:28.340 --> 01:02:30.330
And this is a--

01:02:30.330 --> 01:02:32.150
it's out of control.

01:02:32.150 --> 01:02:33.080
It's insane.

01:02:33.080 --> 01:02:35.230
Their numbers they're
putting up make no sense.

01:02:35.230 --> 01:02:37.250
It's beyond arbitrary
what they're

01:02:37.250 --> 01:02:40.620
saying are these guidelines
and measures to open.

01:02:40.620 --> 01:02:42.440
And so the answer is--

01:02:42.440 --> 01:02:43.580
and this is beginning.

01:02:43.580 --> 01:02:47.540
There is now scrutiny as
to who these people are

01:02:47.540 --> 01:02:49.970
and who are in these
positions, because they never

01:02:49.970 --> 01:02:51.350
had any impact before.

01:02:51.350 --> 01:02:53.420
They were really
nonentities in a sense,

01:02:53.420 --> 01:02:57.110
at least not impactful
in our daily lives.

01:02:57.110 --> 01:03:01.550
They have created,
by their actions,

01:03:01.550 --> 01:03:03.290
a spotlight on themselves.

01:03:03.290 --> 01:03:05.570
And that is the
answer is that we

01:03:05.570 --> 01:03:08.585
need to make sure that we
are on top of these people.

01:03:08.585 --> 01:03:09.710
These people are officials.

01:03:09.710 --> 01:03:13.340
They're not in charge unless
we let them be in charge.

01:03:13.340 --> 01:03:15.570
So this is sort of
a gradual process.

01:03:15.570 --> 01:03:17.060
It's an education for all of us.

01:03:17.060 --> 01:03:18.950
No one knew about these people.

01:03:18.950 --> 01:03:20.960
I don't think any
of us had ever,

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:23.670
you know, interacted
with these people before.

01:03:23.670 --> 01:03:27.230
So we need to make sure
that we are holding

01:03:27.230 --> 01:03:30.630
these officials accountable,
even at the local level

01:03:30.630 --> 01:03:32.780
not just the state
level, the local level.

01:03:32.780 --> 01:03:37.358
They have tremendous
control of your lives.

01:03:37.358 --> 01:03:39.840
[APPLAUSE]

01:03:39.840 --> 01:03:43.040
SPEAKER 2: We have time
for one more question.

01:03:43.040 --> 01:03:45.600
AUDIENCE: Yes, Dr. Atlas,
thank you for being here.

01:03:45.600 --> 01:03:48.060
It's a pleasure to hear
your expertise this evening.

01:03:48.060 --> 01:03:50.810
I'm just wondering,
as one who is choosing

01:03:50.810 --> 01:03:54.860
not to get the vaccine, could
you possibly give your opinion

01:03:54.860 --> 01:03:57.980
or speak to the effectiveness
of hydroxychloroquine

01:03:57.980 --> 01:04:00.643
or ivermectin as treatment?

01:04:00.643 --> 01:04:01.310
SCOTT ATLAS: OK.

01:04:01.310 --> 01:04:05.180
We're going to hit
all these hot topics.

01:04:05.180 --> 01:04:10.310
Yeah, I mean, OK, so
there's a lot of controversy

01:04:10.310 --> 01:04:12.380
about all these drugs.

01:04:12.380 --> 01:04:14.630
I'll give you a little bit
of my view of what happened

01:04:14.630 --> 01:04:15.680
with hydroxychloroquine.

01:04:15.680 --> 01:04:18.290
What happened with
hydroxychloroquine was,

01:04:18.290 --> 01:04:22.910
A, we had a radioactive
president prematurely say,

01:04:22.910 --> 01:04:26.650
this is absolutely magic.

01:04:26.650 --> 01:04:31.010
A tremendous amount
of internal hostility

01:04:31.010 --> 01:04:33.770
toward the president
inside the administration,

01:04:33.770 --> 01:04:39.080
massive, shocking, that
was going to do anything it

01:04:39.080 --> 01:04:40.010
could to block that.

01:04:40.010 --> 01:04:42.410
This is my opinion.

01:04:42.410 --> 01:04:47.300
And then, there was a
lot of premature data

01:04:47.300 --> 01:04:50.750
that came out that was not--
that was simply like anecdotal.

01:04:50.750 --> 01:04:54.410
And poor studies
were then done that

01:04:54.410 --> 01:04:56.540
were looking at
it in late stage,

01:04:56.540 --> 01:04:59.330
or later stage,
disease, where no one--

01:04:59.330 --> 01:05:01.040
most people did not
think that's when

01:05:01.040 --> 01:05:03.030
the drug would be effective.

01:05:03.030 --> 01:05:07.160
And so it got-- it got sort of
a steamrolled negative thing.

01:05:07.160 --> 01:05:09.290
If you read, there's
a couple of papers

01:05:09.290 --> 01:05:12.300
by Joe Ladapo and others.

01:05:12.300 --> 01:05:16.370
He's a UCLA physician who did
a compilation of the research

01:05:16.370 --> 01:05:18.200
on hydroxychloroquine.

01:05:18.200 --> 01:05:21.050
And it's pretty good data.

01:05:21.050 --> 01:05:24.830
And there's a lot of studies
out that show that it seems--

01:05:24.830 --> 01:05:26.745
I'm not an expert on
that data, by the way.

01:05:26.745 --> 01:05:28.870
I haven't really spent a
lot of time looking at it.

01:05:28.870 --> 01:05:32.930
It seems that it's effective
in early disease and possibly,

01:05:32.930 --> 01:05:37.310
but we don't know, it's at least
being studied for prophylaxis.

01:05:37.310 --> 01:05:40.760
Like you take, and I have taken
hydroxychloroquine for malaria

01:05:40.760 --> 01:05:44.450
prophylaxis many years ago.

01:05:44.450 --> 01:05:46.550
But it's thought,
if it's effective,

01:05:46.550 --> 01:05:50.090
it's effective in
early stage disease.

01:05:50.090 --> 01:05:52.170
Ivermectin I don't
know much about.

01:05:52.170 --> 01:05:56.000
But it's sort of-- there's
pretty, very positive data

01:05:56.000 --> 01:05:58.873
about it that again,
a lot of these studies

01:05:58.873 --> 01:06:00.290
are criticized
because they're not

01:06:00.290 --> 01:06:03.840
these perfect, randomized,
controlled studies.

01:06:03.840 --> 01:06:05.780
But, as we all
know, haven't seen

01:06:05.780 --> 01:06:07.490
a lot of randomized
controlled studies

01:06:07.490 --> 01:06:09.900
about masks and 6-foot
social distancing.

01:06:09.900 --> 01:06:13.970
[CHEERING]

01:06:13.970 --> 01:06:16.340
By the way, just sort
of an interesting aside,

01:06:16.340 --> 01:06:18.048
it has nothing to do
with their question.

01:06:18.048 --> 01:06:22.460
But the WHO says three feet, and
many countries use three feet.

01:06:22.460 --> 01:06:23.790
Now why is that important?

01:06:23.790 --> 01:06:26.000
It's important to know
because, A, it shows

01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:28.610
how arbitrary the rule is.

01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:30.807
It's not that three feet
is the right number,

01:06:30.807 --> 01:06:31.640
I'm not saying that.

01:06:31.640 --> 01:06:35.240
But it also shows, if
it's three feet, that's

01:06:35.240 --> 01:06:38.143
a game changer for a
restaurant, for instance.

01:06:38.143 --> 01:06:39.560
You know, because
three feet away,

01:06:39.560 --> 01:06:41.143
I mean, unless you're
with the person,

01:06:41.143 --> 01:06:43.238
you're not sitting three
feet, you know, usually.

01:06:43.238 --> 01:06:44.780
I mean there are
certain restaurants.

01:06:44.780 --> 01:06:47.240
So these kinds of
things are just

01:06:47.240 --> 01:06:50.690
pointing out how arbitrary
these rules have been.

01:06:50.690 --> 01:06:53.360
It's clear social
distancing will eliminate

01:06:53.360 --> 01:06:55.640
and will stop the
spread of an infection.

01:06:55.640 --> 01:06:58.700
And my analogy is, if I'm in
Paris and you're in London,

01:06:58.700 --> 01:07:00.618
you're breathing the
same air generally.

01:07:00.618 --> 01:07:01.910
But you're not going to get it.

01:07:01.910 --> 01:07:02.868
You're far enough away.

01:07:02.868 --> 01:07:04.640
Now, I don't know
about six feet.

01:07:04.640 --> 01:07:05.690
No one knows.

01:07:05.690 --> 01:07:08.990
It's never been proven.

01:07:08.990 --> 01:07:10.880
And there's a lot
of horror stories

01:07:10.880 --> 01:07:13.992
about how the 6-foot rule came
about in that situation room.

01:07:13.992 --> 01:07:15.450
But it happened
before I was there.

01:07:15.450 --> 01:07:17.570
So I won't claim to know that.

01:07:17.570 --> 01:07:20.720
But it's a joke.

01:07:20.720 --> 01:07:25.220
The drug studies
have been perverted.

01:07:25.220 --> 01:07:30.560
The whole climate has been
destroyed by the politics.

01:07:30.560 --> 01:07:32.270
And it's very sad.

01:07:32.270 --> 01:07:34.880
Because, frankly, in
my opinion, people

01:07:34.880 --> 01:07:39.050
were killed because of the
politics of stopping the drug

01:07:39.050 --> 01:07:40.970
data from coming out.

01:07:40.970 --> 01:07:47.110
[APPLAUSE]

01:07:47.110 --> 01:07:48.110
SPEAKER 2: Please join--

01:07:48.110 --> 01:07:50.330
please join me in
thanking Dr. Atlas.

01:07:50.330 --> 01:07:53.680
[APPLAUSE]

